Random number generation
------------------------

the rand() function returns a pseudo-random integer in the range 0 to RAND_MAX inclusive.

the srand() function sets its argument as the seed for a new sequence of pseudo-random integeres to be returned by rand(). These sequences are repeatable by calling srand() with the same seed value.

If no seed value is provided, the rand() function is automatically seeded with a value of 1.  
